        "chunks": [
          {
            "chunk_type": "isnad",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "From him, from ʿAlī ibn Ismāʿīl, from Ḥammād ibn ʿĪsā, who said:",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 10,
            "word_start": 0
          },
          {
            "chunk_type": "body",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Yaqṭīn wrote to al-ʿAbd al-Ṣāliḥ عليه السلام: “May a man perform the salat (prayer) while wearing an izār wrapped around himself over the qamīṣ?” So he wrote: “Yes.”",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 33,
            "word_start": 10
          },
          {
            "chunk_type": "closing",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "Thus, the import of these reports is the lifting of prohibition and permissibility, while the earlier reports pertain to virtue and recommendation; and there is no contradiction between them.",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 48,
            "word_start": 33
          }
        ],
